Author: Mike Reid <mike.reid@canterbury.ac.nz>
Date:   Mon Jun 1 10:50:48 2026 +1200

    ZEFOZ: per-thread coefficients and thread-safety fixes; correct Newton update scaling

    - Allocate a per-thread coefficient vector (zd_inst->coeff) and copy initial coefficients from the shared Hamiltonian to avoid concurrent writes to h->coeff\n- Add zhd_with_coeff() to evaluate the Hamiltonian with an explicit coefficient vector (avoids mutating h->coeff)\n- Use omp_get_max_threads() to size per-thread workspaces to avoid OOB when OMP_NUM_THREADS > num_procs\n- Correct Newton update scaling: apply 0.5 * C^{-1} v (d2 returns half the Hessian)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

